// An authored `+` over bare `u32` must not enter a domain predicate's
// membership proof. A domain predicate's `self` is the bare carrier, so the
// only authored operator that could apply there joins the primitive `u32`
// family, and stage 02 now refuses that declaration outright: only the core
// semantic-home owner may publish a primitive operator meaning. The rejection
// therefore lands at the declaration, before any membership proof, and this
// control now pins the same refusal as the operator-home forgery controls.
boundary machine + Integer::replace(left: u32, right: u32) -> u32;
domain u32::Clear
    requires ((self + 0) & 2) == 0;
machine main() -> u32 in Clear { 0 as u32 in Clear }
